                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_15\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes FileHandler.java's visitFile method from:\n  String tempPath = fileName.toString();\nto:\n  String tempPath = location.relativize(path).toString();\nin order to keep the relative path (directory structure) instead of just the bare filename when populating the spec/config dropdown.\n\nTracing the history of this exact line across the candidates shows the following evolution of `tempPath`:\n- candidate_04 (introduction of fileMatcher/visitFile): `String tempPath = path.toString().replaceAll(location + \"/\", \"\");` \u2014 full relative path preserved.\n- candidate_07: adds `.toLowerCase()`.\n- candidate_10: wraps with `StringHandler.toCamelCase(...)`.\n- candidate_11: reverts the toCamelCase wrapping.\n- candidate_12: re-adds toCamelCase.\n- candidate_13: reverts toCamelCase again.\n- candidate_14: switches `location + \"/\"` to `location + File.separator`.\n- candidate_15: rewrites the method signature to take a `Path location` instead of `String location`, changes the match target from `path` to `fileName = path.getFileName()`, and critically replaces the line with `String tempPath = fileName.toString();` \u2014 this discards the relative path entirely and keeps only the bare filename, matching the buggy code shown as removed (`-`) in fix_commit_diff.txt exactly.\n- candidate_16 is the fix commit itself, which restores relative-path behavior via `location.relativize(path).toString()`.\n\nSince candidate_15's `String tempPath = fileName.toString();` is byte-for-byte identical to the pre-fix buggy line, and it is the commit that first introduced this exact code (by switching from matching against the full relative path to matching/extracting only the filename), candidate_15 is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
